      "content": "There is a discernible difference in the *expectations* of business conduct, though this is a generalization. The Nigerian landscape can sometimes operate more informally, where navigating relationships and local networks is key to procedural success, which some perceive as less formalized. Conversely, the operating environment in Southeast Asia, including Vietnam, tends to have more established commercial expectations built into their manufacturing processes. Ultimately, both regions require due diligence, but the nature of the risk—informality versus infrastructure—differs significantly.",
